ng used outside of tests."]],0,110],[7169988,20411,15,0.692,0.487,[[23,0.765,4,12],[24,0.235,0,3]],[["fa5b9d89_a69b454d",22,0,1,"nit: Say: \"Make DeviceInfo.setForTesting methods apply to native code\""]],0,111],[7209649,20419,27,0.796,0.667,[[24,0.6,2,16],[25,0.225,0,6],[26,0.1,0,3],[27,0.075,0,2]],[["ea0e13cd_3d41be64",23,0,0,"guess that wasn't so difficult :P"]],0,115],[7209653,20420,43,1.21,0.931,[[26,0.735,1,34],[28,0.122,1,4],[29,0.082,0,3],[30,0.061,2,2]],[["f77a8402_d856db71",22,0,1,"nit: this is pretty vague. Suggest: \"Do not add DEFINE_JNI macros for generate_jar_jni\""]],0,119],[7217970,20424,33,1.326,1.047,[[31,0.231,2,8],[32,0.205,6,7],[33,0.179,2,6],[26,0.179,3,6],[24,0.128,4,4],[34,0.077,2,2]],[],0,122],[7092856,20426,553,9.596,7.813,[[35,0.213,4,124],[3,0.119,25,68],[0,0.107,25,58],[36,0.099,0,57],[32,0.091,7,52],[37,0.068,0,39],[38,0.061,0,36],[39,0.046,2,25],[8,0.033,17,17],[40,0.033,1,18],[41,0.017,1,8],[42,0.017,0,8],[7,0.017,3,9],[43,0.013,3,6],[44,0.012,6,6],[45,0.012,0,5],[6,0.01,10,4],[46,0.01,0,5],[47,0.008,0,4],[23,0.007,5,3],[48,0.005,5,2],[49,0.003,0,1]],[["2d95568f_b8ef8668",24,-9,1,"nit: add a comment: ``` // Allows test classes to set features & command-line before Finch is initialized. ```"],["3bb2e8ee_95f92fdc",25,-9,1,"Wonder if it'd make sense to just use `BuildConfig.IS_FOR_TEST` instead?"],["3e025e58_8b8b3847",26,-9,1,"nit: add comment: ``` // Tests contained in a class so it can be a friend of ... ```"],["3e829073_e8c02f35",27,-9,1,"nit: add comment: ``` // When this is enabled, these things will have already been initialized. ```"],["5a6aefe2_247c346f",28,-9,1,"nit: probably no point in having this field now. Just return `ChromeFeatureListCreator::GetInstance()` from the getter."],["6e53f26f_51da8a6d",24,-9,1,"nit: add comment: ``` // Allows test classes to set the locale before Finch is initialized. ```"],["945e9d63_f876ce02",24,-9,1,"nit: might be slicker to add when changing the locale: ``` Locale prevLocale = Locale.getDefault(); ResettersForTesting.register(() -> Locale.setDefault(prevLocale)); ```"],["a082da0c_3cfec74f",29,-9,1,"I think we're meant to have //components not depend on //chrome. Probably should move InitializeFinch into //chrome somewhere."],["b943cf78_ff8775b5",30,-9,1,"nit: add a comment about why we need these."],["baf00670_a8e064fd",31,-9,1,"do you know how?"],["d5483198_7c79b9be",32,-9,1,"nit: Looks like there's both HOST_RESOLVER_RULES and `MockCertVerifierRuleAndroid` that set command-lines. It's not obvious from CS why either of them would be read by finch. If you could elaborate…"],["1c701a42_84ac4d3f",33,-2,1,"Mention this is experimental and maybe TODO-associate with a tracking bug?"],["66716431_273a8800",34,-2,1,"This needs a comment. What does this actually do? A scoped feature list is scoped, but this does not provide any scoping mechanism. (i.e. there's no manual destroy function) Is it OK to call this…"],["7095d694_bd236c77",35,-2,1,"Nit: No need for content:: when we're in content namespace. Same below."],["a9e20e4f_c4305897",36,-2,1,"It's unclear why these short wrappers are needed. Is it for some DEPS validation - i.e. we don't want to expose the more specific headers more broadly than needed? If so, add a comment. Also, each of…"],["c472e10f_faac3609",26,-2,1,"I think it would be helpful to separate the otherwise no-op refactoring to separate CLs, so if there's any reverts/relands needed, they can be minimal in size and won't need to carry big refactoring…"],["17f15eab_d2df4594",37,-1,0,"This comment and code makes me worried that something might not be fully working in this codepath. Have you verified that we're able to fetch new Finch seeds after starting this way? We don't want a…"],["197eda93_50795f25",38,-1,1,"This should now be made private. If it would be a big change, can make it a TODO for now."],["4883b906_5df346a5",34,-1,1,"Thanks for this comment. Can you expand a bit more to talk to the \"scoped\" nature and how it interacts with calling multiple times. Something like: Internally, this manages a single…"],["c85f206d_3b646820",39,-1,1,"Looking how this is called: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc;drc=b2d540b15cad394746b9277911ae1192f25158aa;l=7275 It seems…"],["da901107_f7b39236",28,-1,1,"If we end up sticking with this approach, we should refactor code to remove this. Let's add a TODO."],["fabf4062_e7c4aacc",38,-1,1,"Can you add a comment about this or on the class itself about the lifetime? i.e. it gets created on first access through this API. And that construction is generally a no-op until CreateFeatureList()…"],["7a661c94_9ec16438",40,0,1,"Nit: Move to match the .h order."]],0,125],[7247787,20432,35,1.144,0.818,[[48,0.333,6,12],[41,0.222,2,8],[0,0.156,26,5],[6,0.156,11,5],[46,0.133,1,5]],[],0,126],[7231150,20433,532,9.596,7.813,[[35,0.224,5,124],[3,0.125,26,68],[0,0.104,27,54],[36,0.104,1,57],[32,0.095,8,52],[37,0.071,1,39],[38,0.064,1,36],[39,0.049,3,25],[40,0.038,2,20],[8,0.035,18,17],[42,0.017,1,8],[7,0.017,4,9],[43,0.014,4,6],[44,0.012,7,6],[45,0.012,1,5],[47,0.009,1,4],[23,0.007,6,3],[49,0.003,1,1]],[],0,127],[7262533,20438,532,9.596,7.813,[[35,0.224,6,124],[3,0.125,27,68],[0,0.104,28,54],[36,0.104,2,57],[32,0.095,9,52],[37,0.071,2,39],[38,0.064,2,36],[39,0.049,4,25],[40,0.038,3,20],[8,0.035,19,17],[42,0.017,2,8],[7,0.017,5,9],[43,0.014,5,6],[44,0.012,8,6],[45,0.012,2,5],[47,0.009,2,4],[23,0.007,7,3],[49,0.003,2,1]],[],0,128],[7248309,20438,1307,8.899,7.191,[[29,0.899,2,1184],[32,0.036,9,46],[50,0.023,0,29],[26,0.02,4,24],[24,0.011,5,13],[51,0.005,2,4],[52,0.004,3,4],[53,0.003,1,3]],[["4d80b9bc_353d4bdd",23,-1,1,"Can you move this to `jni_zero_internal.h` since it's not meant to be called by devs directly?"],["611f0385_33ca99d7",23,-1,1,"I'm not 100% on this, but I believe this should be \"inline auto\"."],["976a64c3_23ed2f25",41,-1,1,"Can you add comments here (copy from commit description) explaining why we need th